      "prompt": "At Northwind Analytics, our designers create custom UI for replenishment workflows that must be intuitive for regional grocery staff. How do you approach the initial design hand-off phase to ensure that your technical constraints are understood while still respecting the designer's vision for the user experience?",
      "answer_outline": "The candidate should describe a collaborative approach, such as early involvement in the design process, asking clarifying questions about user flows, and providing constructive feedback on technical feasibility early on. They should emphasize building a partnership rather than a transactional hand-off.",
